/target
**/target
Cargo.lock.bak

# Build products. packaging/out is binaries, packages and the assembled
# repository tree -- hundreds of megabytes, all reproducible from a tag.
/packaging/out/

# Signing keys. These are the one thing here that cannot be regenerated without
# every user re-trusting a new key, so they are kept out of the repository and
# backed up out of band. See packaging/repo/README.md.
/packaging/repo/keys/

# Third-party binaries the Windows installer bundles, and the installer itself.
# NSSM is public domain but not ours to redistribute from a git tree, and the
# .exe is a build product -- packaging/windows/fetch-vendor.ps1 gets one and
# build-installer.ps1 makes the other.
/packaging/windows/vendor/
/packaging/windows/Breeze-Core-Setup.exe
